// A struct with a struct field and a fixed array of owners: a `move` or a `del` vacates the owners
// that it can overlap, and a use names the first owner that the read reads and that can be vacated,
// numbered in the type of the read or of the local.
string[47] NESTED = {
    // a `del` of `t.e[0]` vacates `t.e[1]` and keeps `t.p.a`: P1 U1d0.1
    "fn main.n1(_1 (t): outer) -> void {",
